Problem: Many people have story ideas but lack the drawing or writing skills to turn them into visuals. Commissioning artwork is slow and costly.

Idea: A web app where the user types a short story idea, picks a genre, art style and panel count, and gets a finished illustrated comic page.

Target users: students, hobbyist writers, teachers making visual stories, and content creators who want quick storyboards.

Ideas considered:

Text-only story generator (rejected: not visual enough)
Single-image generator (rejected: no narrative)
Multi-panel comic with captions and dialogue (chosen)

Unique value: one prompt produces script, dialogue and art, with control over genre and style (Manga, Noir ink, Watercolor, etc.).

Expected outcome: a comic of 2–8 panels that can be printed or saved as JSON.
